 <main class="meet"><nav class="hub-subnav wrap" aria-label="In About"><span class="hub-subnav-label">IN ABOUT</span><a href="/about/">Overview</a><a href="/abilities/">Abilities</a><a href="/meet-atlas" aria-current="page">Meet Atlas</a><a href="/what-is-atlas/">What is Atlas</a><a href="/why-atlas/">Why Atlas</a></nav><div class="in"><p class="eyebrow">MEET ATLAS</p><h1>A continuous intelligence for a world that does not fit in one chat.</h1><p class="lead">Atlas is being built to carry forward the people, projects, decisions, sources and unfinished work you choose to keep, while letting the model underneath her change.</p>
 <div class="meet-grid"><section class="meet-card"><h2>What exists today</h2><p>Atlas already has working local continuity, a desktop shell, governed routing and evidence-backed pieces of the wider system. The Abilities page carries the current evidence status for each public claim.</p></section><section class="meet-card"><h2>What this page is not</h2><p>This is not a live chat, signup flow or provider connection. No account is created and no message leaves this page. It is a public explanation of the product while those service paths are still being built and accepted.</p></section><section class="meet-card"><h2>Your history stays governed</h2><p>Memory is not permission. Connected information and actions are designed to remain scoped to the authority you grant, with receipts for governed work and visible holds when a required boundary is not ready.</p></section><section class="meet-card"><h2>One Atlas, different ways to work</h2><p>Research, design, coding and media can change the tools around Atlas without creating another identity. Rooms, Projects, Life and Realm are views into the same continuing person.</p></section><section class="meet-card"><h2>An enhanced definition of Digital Engineering</h2><p>The engineering behind an Atlas built around your life: at Titan, we have enhanced the definition of DIGITAL ENGINEERING — connecting ideas from biology, mathematics, quantum science and planetary science with software engineering and design to create coherent, useful systems around human life. The same standard governs what she reports, what she holds, and what she refuses to fake. <a href="/digital-engineering/">Explore our approach →</a></p></section></div>
 <p class="meet-note"><strong>Demonstration boundary:</strong> examples on the public site illustrate intended behaviour. They are not recordings of your data and do not imply an unconnected backend is live.</p>
